 {
  "name": "X9 extern combines with packed",
  "file": "compiler/src/particle.cpp",
  "old": "&&!externStruct&&!packedStruct&&!opaqueStruct) { p++; externStruct=true;",
  "new": "&&!externStruct) { p++; externStruct=true;",
  "tests": [
   "tests/cp09_linkage.py"
  ],
  "equivalent": "the `packed` and `opaque` modifier lines only continue when the next token is `struct` or the other of the two, never `extern`, so no modifier can precede `extern struct`; and the `extern` line only fires when the next token is `struct`, so `extern packed struct` / `extern opaque struct` never reach it. The guard on packedStruct/opaqueStruct is therefore never false-by-flag at that point: with or without it the same sources parse (the combinations are a parse error)."
 },
